# Rank 1552 / CVE-2022-2216: parse-url delegated its URL parsing to
# the parse-path dependency and pinned a version carrying
# CVE-2022-2215 -- parse-path before 5.0.0 mishandles URLs whose
# protocol appears more than once (javascript://javascript:alert)
# and whose credentials contain encoded characters, so every
# parse-url consumer inherited the parsing bypass (vulnerable
# dependency, CWE-1104/CWE-20; fixed by upgrading, no code change in
# parse-url itself). The refactor commit changed package.json from
# `"parse-path": "^4.0.4"` to `"parse-path": "^5.0.0"` (and is-ssh,
# protocols similarly). the fixing commit is the fixing change
# (confirmed, "Refactor codebase, upgrade dependencies"; the
# library's own lib/index.js logic is untouched apart from
# comments). .
#
# ATTENTION, vulnerable-dependency reachability. The corpus's SCA
# family (VYQL-SCA-002 ReachableVulnerableDependency) judges
# manifest-to-advisory pairings through the scanner's SCA extraction
# on real dependency graphs -- in a spec snippet there is no lockfile
# or advisory database to reason over, so both directions assert
# reject: the pair records that a pinned parse-path ^4.0.4 with the
# library's parsing entry point is the shape SCA-002 must eventually
# report, and the ^5.0.0 bump is the clearing form. Measured on the
# real code: scanning lib/index.js reports zero findings at both
# revisions (the vulnerability is in the dependency, not this
# file). No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No definition change shipped.
# Spec cve_rank1552 records the manifest pinning the vulnerable
# parser and the upgraded pin, both asserting reject VYQL-SCA-002:
# when spec-level dependency vocabulary lands, the ^4 pin must flip
# to expect.

test "rank1552: the manifest pins the vulnerable parser"
  lang javascript
  file package.json
  reject VYQL-SCA-002
  code
  ```
  {
    "name": "parse-url",
    "version": "6.0.0",
    "description": "Parse urls and preprocess them.",
    "main": "lib/index.js",
    "dependencies": {
      "is-ssh": "^1.3.0",
      "parse-path": "^4.0.4",
      "protocols": "^1.4.0"
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1552: the fixed revision bumps past the vulnerable parser"
  lang javascript
  file package.json
  reject VYQL-SCA-002
  code
  ```
  {
    "name": "parse-url",
    "version": "7.0.0",
    "description": "Parse urls and preprocess them.",
    "main": "lib/index.js",
    "dependencies": {
      "is-ssh": "^1.4.0",
      "parse-path": "^5.0.0",
      "protocols": "^2.0.1"
    }
  }
  ```
